{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide takes you from a wired Swidux app to a fully gated feature with paywall presentation, entitlement observation, restore, and manage-subscription support. It covers state and action wiring, implementing a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", presenting the sheet, gating a feature, and previewing in pro state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For an API-level reference of every type and action, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","type":"reference"},{"text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Before you start","anchor":"Before-you-start"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You have a Swidux app already wired up — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppReducer"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"type":"text","text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" first."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You have a purchase backend in mind. RevenueCat is the path of least resistance, but vanilla StoreKit or a custom server work just as well — the plugin doesn’t care."}]}]}]},{"level":2,"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target in "},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPaywall\",","    ]",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 2: Add state and actions","anchor":"Step-2-Add-state-and-actions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a paywall slice to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a paywall case to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ AppState.swift","import SwiduxPaywall","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var paywall: PaywallState = .init()","    \/\/ … other slices","}"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ AppAction.swift","import SwiduxPaywall","","enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case paywall(PaywallAction)","    \/\/ … other cases","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin owns reducing for ","type":"text"},{"code":".paywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" actions, so the root reducer should fall through:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ AppReducer.swift","case .paywall:","    return nil"]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Step-3-Provide-a-PaywallService","type":"heading","text":"Step 3: Provide a `PaywallService`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin needs a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer that talks to your purchase backend. Pick the path that matches your backend.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Path-A-RevenueCat-recommended","type":"heading","text":"Path A: RevenueCat (recommended)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" companion package and use the supplied "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":". No bridging code on your side."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\", from: \"1.0.0\"),"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","","let service = RevenueCatPaywallService()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The companion package also ships "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"type":"text","text":", a SwiftUI sheet built on RevenueCatUI that hands purchase results back through the plugin. See its README for configuration (API key, entitlement identifiers)."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Path-B-StoreKit-or-custom-backend","type":"heading","text":"Path B: StoreKit or custom backend"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For any non-RevenueCat backend, implement "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. The protocol is small:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxPaywall","","struct MyPaywallService: PaywallService {","    func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot {","        \/\/ Fetch the current entitlement once.","        return EntitlementSnapshot()","    }","","    func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot> {","        AsyncStream { continuation in","            \/\/ Yield a new snapshot each time the entitlement changes.","            \/\/ Call continuation.finish() when the source ends.","        }","    }","","    func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot {","        \/\/ Run a restore against the user's account and return the result.","        return EntitlementSnapshot()","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vanilla StoreKit conformer iterates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transaction.currentEntitlements"},{"type":"text","text":" and listens to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transaction.updates"},{"type":"text","text":"; a custom server conformer hits whatever endpoint reports the user’s entitlement."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Previews-and-tests","type":"heading","text":"Previews and tests"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the built-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" for backend-agnostic previews:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let service = MockPaywallService(isPro: true)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you’re on Path A, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" also ships "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" for RevenueCat-flavored previews."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-4-Wire-the-plugin","level":2,"text":"Step 4: Wire the plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construct and register "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" inside your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"text":" factory:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxPaywall","","let paywallPlugin = PaywallPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.paywall,","    action: AppAction.paywall,","    extractAction: { if case .paywall(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","    service: RevenueCatPaywallService()",")","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 5: Observe customer info on launch","anchor":"Step-5-Observe-customer-info-on-launch","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Start the long-lived entitlement stream once, on the root view:"}]},{"code":["struct ContentView: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","","    var body: some View {","        RootContent()","            .task { store.send(.paywall(.observeCustomerInfo)) }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeCustomerInfo"},{"text":" returns an effect that lives for the duration of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService.customerInfoStream()"},{"text":". Every snapshot the service yields flows through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".customerInfoUpdated"},{"text":" and updates ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.isPro"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPermanentLicense"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 6: Present the paywall","anchor":"Step-6-Present-the-paywall","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Bind a sheet to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.isPresented"},{"text":" and dispatch ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".paywall(.dismiss)"},{"text":" when it closes:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".sheet(isPresented: Binding(","    get: { store.paywall.isPresented },","    set: { if !$0 { store.send(.paywall(.dismiss)) } }",")) {","    PaywallSheet()","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Trigger presentation by dispatching "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".paywall(.request(reason:))"},{"type":"text","text":" with a short identifier describing why you’re asking. The reason is stored in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.requestedReason"},{"type":"text","text":" so the sheet can tailor its copy."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["store.send(.paywall(.request(reason: \"export-pdf\")))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 7: Gate a feature","anchor":"Step-7-Gate-a-feature"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState.isGateSatisfied"},{"type":"text","text":" before running gated work. If it’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", dispatch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request"},{"type":"text","text":" instead:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Button(\"Export PDF\") {","    if store.paywall.isGateSatisfied {","        store.send(.export(.exportPDF))","    } else {","        store.send(.paywall(.request(reason: \"export-pdf\")))","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 8: Restore purchases","anchor":"Step-8-Restore-purchases","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a restore button to your paywall sheet. Reflect "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.isLoading"},{"type":"text","text":" to disable it while the call is in flight:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Button(\"Restore Purchases\") {","    store.send(.paywall(.restorePurchases))","}",".disabled(store.paywall.isLoading)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On success, the resulting snapshot flows through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":" and updates the gate. On failure, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.error"},{"type":"text","text":" is set."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 9: Manage subscriptions","anchor":"Step-9-Manage-subscriptions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For an existing subscriber, surface a button that deep-links into the system subscription management page:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Button(\"Manage Subscription\") {","    store.send(.paywall(.openManageSubscriptions))","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This opens "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"itms-apps:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions"},{"type":"text","text":" via the plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openURL"},{"type":"text","text":" handler, which routes to the App Store on iOS and Settings on macOS."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Testing","anchor":"Testing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" to drive previews and tests into a known entitlement state:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["#Preview(\"Pro\") {","    let store = AppStore.configured(","        paywallService: MockPaywallService(isPro: true)","    )","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}","","#Preview(\"Free\") {","    let store = AppStore.configured(","        paywallService: MockPaywallService()","    )","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plumb the service through a parameter on your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"type":"text","text":" factory so previews can override it without touching the live RevenueCat SDK."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Add a Paywall","role":"article"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall"]}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"title":"How-to Guides"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","abstract":[{"text":"Install the bundled ","type":"text"},{"code":"swidux-ref","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand.","type":"text"}],"title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify.","type":"text"}],"title":"Add Analytics","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","title":"Getting Started with Swidux","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"title":"Add a Parental Gate","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","abstract":[{"text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store.","type":"text"}],"title":"Add a Version Killswitch","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"title":"Plugin Architecture","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"https://github.com/heirloomlogic/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall":{"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}],"title":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config.","type":"text"}],"title":"Add Feature Flags","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags"}}}